WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.834
-Bizarrap. Do I call you Bizarrap or Biza?

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.701
Or -- What do I call you? -It's fine.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.801
Biza, for you, is okay.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.100
-[ Laughs ] For me, it's okay. Yeah.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.100
And I'm going to call you Shakira, obviously.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.467
Welcome back. -"Shak."

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.300
-I can call you Shak, as well, yeah, of course.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.334
Congratulations. "Music Sessions, Volume 53."

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:21.934
This is a global monster of a song.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.934
Number one globally!

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:26.968
[ Cheers and applause ] Number one globally.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.567
Couldn't -- I mean, couldn't be a bigger song.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.634
This is the truth. This happened today.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.400
You and Biza,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.234
here are four Guinness World Records you shattered.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.200
And then -- And then you went on -- Shakira --

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.567
went on and won 10 more Guinness World Records.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.400
I'm not kidding. Look at this. Look at this!

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.501
Look at all -- Look at you guys.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:59.634
Most viewed -- Most viewed Latin track on YouTube in 24 hours.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.634
Fastest Latin track to reach 100 million views on YouTube.

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:05.267
Most streamed Latin track on Spotify in 24 hours.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.934
Most streamed Latin track on Spotify in one week.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.634
You crushed it.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.934
You crushed it!

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:16.667
Uh, how did this song come together?

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.434
Did you know Biza? Did you know Shakira?

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:23.501
-Well, you know, my son, Milan, who just turned 10.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.667
-I love --

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.434
By the way, they're so excited to be here.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.434
They're like -- I told them, "Guess what.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.834
We're going to New York." And they said,

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.767
"Are we going to Fallon?!" I said, "Yeah."

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.367
And they started, "Fallon! Fallon! Fallon!"

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.434
-That's my boy. I love those two.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.567
They're the cutest, and they're the most polite kids.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.100
I love them. Every time I see them,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.767
they're so nice. So they hooked you up?

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.901
-Okay, yeah, so -- Yeah, well, actually, you know,

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.534
they're like my career consultants lately.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.434
-Yeah, of course. -They pitch in for video ideas.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:49.734
I listen to everything they say

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.901
because they actually have really good taste.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:55.133
But I'm not objective, you know? -Yeah, of course not.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.701
-And Milan -- he's also a musician.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.868
He has a very good ear, very good taste.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.734
And he's a big Biza fan.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:04.467
And he told me, "Mom..."

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.167
Like, a few months ago, he told me,

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.734
"Mom, you've got to collaborate with Bizarrap.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.200
You have to get on a song with Bizarrap

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.133
because you guys are gonna be number one."

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.901
And he sent a voice note to my manager, Jaime.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:19.601
He said, "Jaime, you got to put my mom together with Bizarrap

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.601
on a song because they're gonna be number one."

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.067
And he was right.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.868
-He called it. I love that he called it.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.300
-I still have that audio.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.934
-You have the voicemail. -Yeah.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:34.067
-What's your version of this story, Biza?

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.868
-I was thinking about the collaboration

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.234
between Shakira and me, but I didn't know

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.133
how to reach her because she's --

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.100
-She's Shakira. -She's a superstar.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.033
-You have to put a light up in the sky

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.834
and hope that Shakira swings in.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.467
She's a superhero. Yeah.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:53.133
-By that time, I think it was July of the past year, 2022.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:55.834
And I had, at that moment --

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:59.834
I had the number-one global song with Quevedo.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.467
He's a guy from Spain.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.067
-I love that song. It's amazing.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:07.667
-And I thought, like, this is a moment to send her a DM.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.334
-To introduce yourself to Shakira.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.601
-Yeah. -He DM'd me.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.434
-You slid into her DMs? -Yeah.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.868
-Yeah, but I didn't see his until, like, three months later.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:20.234
I don't know why. -Yeah, one or two months later.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:21.334
-Yeah, two months later.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.067
-And I remember it was --

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.234
-You made him wait two months?

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.467
-Yeah, but it wasn't on purpose.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.834
-Yeah, we don't answer every DM back.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.100
-Yeah, of course. -She's Shakira. Yeah.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.701
-And it was August, I remember because it was my birthday,

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.634
and I -- We were in the studio.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.634
-It was your birthday? -Yeah, I remember that.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.467
I started my -- We were in the studio,

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.267
and I started my birthday with Shakira

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.434
singing me the "Happy Birthday."

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:44.767
-Ohh! -Do you remember that?

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.300
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -How cool.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.801
-Yeah, yeah. That was -- -But what do you --

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:51.267
What's your pitch when you're DMing Shakira?

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:54.834
Like, "Let's do a song together. Let's collaborate."

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.767
-Yeah. I told her, like,

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.367
"I would really like to collab with you."

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:02.167
And I had that -- that big song out there.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.734
-Yeah, and you were like, "That's me."

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:05.000
-Yeah. "That's me."

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.934
-That was very easy, actually.

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.367
-Yeah, but you made him wait two months

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.033
before even answering back.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.734
-But after I heard that he actually DM'd me,

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.667
then I wrote him back.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.634
And, you know, I showed Milan.

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.968
I said, "Look who's writing to Mommy!"

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:23.334
And he said, "Oh, my God! The Argentinian God!"

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:24.534
-Oh, really? -Yeah.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.467
-The Argentinian God? -The Argentinian God.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:30.367
-And, Biza, when you have those, did you think of a beat

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.601
immediately and you go like, "This is the one for Shakira"?

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.334
And then how do you just go -- You don't just say yes to it.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.300
Do you go, "Hey, I got some notes,"

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.567
or, "I'm don't know if I'm feeling this"?

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.100
-Well, he came to Barcelona, right?

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.434
-Yeah, I came to Barcelona.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:45.334
And one day before, I made like two beats, I think.

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:49.868
And then when I show the two beats to her,

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:52.467
she told me like, "This is the..."

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.234
-Yeah, because it reminded me kind of like --

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.067
It reminded me of Depeche Mode a little bit.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -Right?

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.534
-Depeche Mode? -Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:05:01.501
This song, if you listen to it, it's got a little bit of that

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:05.033
sort of, like, cool, dark undertone.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:07.100
I love Depeche Mode. It's my favorite.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.300
-Yeah, it has a lot of synths,

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.801
and it sounds like an '80s track, maybe.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:12.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:15.400
-And, yeah, I really love that kind of music.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.067
And I knew that Shakira would love that.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.634
-I started to feel it in my body, you know.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.300
I usually have this visceral

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.834
sort of physical reaction to music.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:28.734
And if you see me, you know, two-stepping,

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.133
things are not right.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.567
You know? Yeah.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:34.767
I know when a song works because then I suddenly start moving,

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.467
like, getting these small contractions

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:41.367
from my tailbone to my iliac bone,

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:45.167
and then it just results into, you know, hip movements.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:48.667
-Are you telling me that your hips don't lie?

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.434
-Yeah. I didn't want to go there.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:52.968
-This is the best thing that ever happened to me!

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:55.367
This is the greatest! I can retire now.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.734
This is all I ever wanted to know,

00:05:57.734 --> 00:06:00.501
is if, really, if your hips do lie or don't lie to you.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:01.634
You're actually telling us --

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.000
-They do not lie. -They do not lie.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.167
-They do not ever. -You can feel it.

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.667
-And I know when a song is right when they start to move.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.901
-Wow! You know what's great about this?

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:13.033
People from all over the world love this song,

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:15.934
but also all ages love this song.

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:19.734
And I have a video here of some fans singing along to the song.

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:21.601
Let's just take a look at this for a second.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:24.000
-[ Singing in Spanish ]

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:33.467
♪♪

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:35.434
-[ Laughs ] -I mean...

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:37.834
-Do you love that? That's got to make you feel good, right?

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:40.634
-Oh, my God. Yeah, it's been amazing.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.701
I'm just waiting for someone to just pinch me

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.634
and wake me up from this dream.

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:48.901
It's unbelievable to feel the reaction from so many people.

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:53.934
I think that people really connect to music

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.701
when it's really genuine, when it's real,

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:58.000
when it comes from a real place. -Yeah.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.501
-And the thing with the song is that it has become sort of

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.734
like an anthem for so many women out there.

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:07.334
You know, I've had a very rough year after my separation.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:12.033
And writing this song has been so important to me.

00:07:12.033 --> 00:07:15.300
It's been a healthy way to channel my emotions.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.300
And I feel that, you know, after we put out this song,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.200
I really felt that I don't even have fans out there.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.801
I have a sisterhood of women

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.067
who have been through the same things

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:28.601
that I have been through, who think the way I think,

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:30.200
who feel the way I feel,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.968
who had to put up with so much crap the way I had to.

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:36.234
And, you know, I did write the song for me,

00:07:36.234 --> 00:07:40.133
but, also, I feel that it was meant to be --

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:43.067
and probably for so many women out there

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:47.000
that needed a forum, too, and a voice to represent them

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.200
in so many ways, so...

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:54.534
-We can't wait to see you perform for us after the break.

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:57.033
Congrats, again, on all the records broken.

00:07:57.033 --> 00:08:00.367
Bizarrap! Shakira!

00:08:00.367 --> 00:08:03.133
"Music Sessions, Volume 53" is out now!

